Consider this C# code:

```csharp
static (Action inc, Func<int> read) Make()
{
    int n = 0;
    return (() => n++, () => n);
}

var (inc, read) = Make();
inc();
inc();
Console.WriteLine(read()); // prints 2
```

`Make` has already returned before `inc` and `read` are called, and `inc` and `read` are two separate delegates. Explain why `read()` still returns `2`.
